<title>USA: EMERGENCY WEATHER CONDITIONS -  WSC - 04-FEB.</title>
<headline>EMERGENCY WEATHER CONDITIONS -  WSC - 04-FEB.</headline>
<text>
<p>Tropical Cyclone Pancho-Helinda, with 90 mph winds, is in the southern Indian Ocean near 19s/86e, moving southeast at 7 mph. The storm will turn more to the southwest with time and weaken. This storm will continue to be a significant threat to shipping until it begins to dissipate by 48-60 hours.</p>
</text>
